course: dictionary
lesson: 15946
title: Unsold: not sold yet
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Unsold means not sold yet. An unsold thing is still in the shop, or still with the seller. The prefix un- means not, so unsold is the same as not sold.
explain: «The bakery had twelve loaves, and nine were sold. The other three loaves were unsold.» To find how many are unsold, take the total and subtract the number sold: 12 − 9 = 3.
explain: Unsold can tell you what happens next. «The unsold bread was given to the food bank.» Unsold things may be thrown away or given away. If they are thrown away, the money spent making them is lost.
fact: Unsold means not sold yet.
fact: «Unsold» is an adjective, so it describes a thing, like «unsold tickets».
fact: To find the unsold amount, use this sum: unsold = total − sold. For example, 20 cakes made and 14 sold means 6 are unsold.
fact: The prefix un- means not, so «unsold» means not sold.
fact: Unsold items may be thrown away or given away, and if they are thrown away, their cost is lost money.
exercise: «The shop had 20 cakes and sold 14.» How many cakes are unsold? | 14 | *6 | 20 | 34
exercise: «The bread was unsold at closing time.» Which word means not sold yet? | *unsold | closing | time | bread
exercise: Ella says unsold means sold out. Why is she wrong? | Unsold means very cheap | Unsold means bought twice | Unsold means sold out, so it is the same | *Unsold means not sold yet, the opposite of sold out
test:
A baker made 30 buns and sold 18. How many buns are unsold? | *12 | 18 | 30 | 48
What does «unsold tickets» mean? | *Tickets nobody has bought yet | Tickets that have been torn up | Tickets for a free show | Tickets bought by two people
exam:
A café made 40 scones, sold 33 and gave the rest to a food bank. How many scones were unsold? | *7 | 33 | 40 | 73
